WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:01.429
Whitebeard

00:00:01.429 --> 00:00:07.589
Even in death, even with half of his head
blown clean away, his body refuses to yield.

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:12.920
His mighty figure, cutting swathes through
his foes, was truly monstrous.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:19.020
Over the course of his battles he received
a full 267 blade wounds, the bullets he endured

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:25.420
total 152, and the cannonballs he has withstood
amount to 46.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:31.430
And yet, upon the proud back of this legendary
man, or indeed upon his very life as a pirate,

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:35.300
he bears no single wound of cowardice.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:41.350
If you wanna find an example of a truly - perfect
supporting character, you need look no further

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:47.200
than Edward Newgate aka Whitebeard and his
role in the story of One Piece.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.920
Oda does a wonderful job of making him one
of THE most badass and influential characters

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.260
in the series.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.140
And he does it in a very interesting way.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:02.190
He introduces Whitebeard as the STRONGEST
pirate in the series, while at the same time

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:08.400
utilising every SINGLE aspect of his character
as a powerful storytelling device.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.580
As you might know, many supporting characters
in your average story usually serve at least

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:19.470
one of two purposes: Make them interact with
the main character so we can engage with them

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:25.060
and thus advance the story, or supply us with
some new piece of information about the world

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.270
our story takes place in.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:30.400
With Whitebeard, Oda does both.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.630
He uses the Emperor to VASTLY expand our understanding
of the one piece world and sets the stage

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.509
for the second half of the plot in the new
world.

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:44.009
And at the SAME time, Oda also fleshes out
his character to be one of THE most important

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:46.660
and powerful players in the story.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:50.990
And I believe that this - was a really smart
move.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:56.170
Because what makes Whitebeard SO popular and
exciting as a character, at least on the surface,

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:00.980
is not what he teaches us about the world,
but who he is as a person.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.909
The strongest man alive.

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:06.040
The pirate respected and feared by all.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.959
And the man who went head to head with the
world government by starting the war of the

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:11.959
best.

00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:16.999
And so I think it’s more than adequate that
in THIS video we will be discussing not one,

00:02:16.999 --> 00:02:21.879
but TWO aspects of Whitebeard’s character:
How he drastically expanded our view of the

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:29.629
One Piece world and why he was the next unofficial
Pirate king after Gol D. Roger.

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:34.909
Before I go and explain how INGENIOUSLY Oda
has used Whitebeard as a world building element

00:02:34.909 --> 00:02:39.519
and how CRITICAL he was in setting up the
second half of the story, I think I first

00:02:39.519 --> 00:02:43.409
have to justify myself for saying that Whitebeard
was the second pirate king.

00:02:43.409 --> 00:02:47.809
That’s a pretty bold statement after all
- believe me, I know.

00:02:47.809 --> 00:02:52.269
But if you bear with me here, I promise it
will ALL make sense once we make it to the

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:53.650
end of this video.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:58.510
So let’s start from zero and steadily build
our way towards pirate king material.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:03.930
Because, to TRULY understand Whitebeard’s
character, we first have to understand the

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:07.359
underlying THEME around which Oda has created
his design.

00:03:07.359 --> 00:03:08.359
Idealism.

00:03:08.359 --> 00:03:13.930
If I made you forget EVERYTHING you knew about
Edward Newgate and his actions in the story,

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:18.329
and THEN asked you to think about what the
IDEAL pirate in one piece for you would look

00:03:18.329 --> 00:03:25.939
like, I bet most people would come up with
either one of two categories: Power or personality.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:30.590
After all what sets Luffy apart from other
characters in the story are pretty much these

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:31.709
2 things.

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:37.549
There are many characters that are as compassionate
and strong-willed as Luffy, and there are

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:41.709
just as many characters that are as strong
or even stronger than him.

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:46.979
And so in the end, what REALLY makes Luffy
so unique, is that he is both.

00:03:46.979 --> 00:03:51.769
However, while Luffy still has to grow as
a person over the course of the story and

00:03:51.769 --> 00:03:58.189
has to train to become stronger, with Whitebeard
Oda shows us what an ideal candidate for pirate

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:00.040
king should look like in the end.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:05.419
I STRONGLY believe, that he’s the ULTIMATE
role model in terms of strength and character

00:04:05.419 --> 00:04:06.959
for Luffy to follow.

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:15.900
So let’s look in detail at how Oda created
Whitebeard within these 2 categories.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:22.490
When Whitebeard was first introduced way back
in chapter 234, Oda gave him the epithet of

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.319
strongest man in the world for a reason.

00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:30.139
While I think it’s fair to debate whether
he was actually stronger than Roger, whether

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:34.930
Kaido as the strongest creature in the world
might have been even more powerful and whether

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:40.980
he was already beyond his prime at Marineford,
I think what isn’t up for debate is that

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:47.840
for at least two DECADES, Edward Newgate was
the most powerful human in the one piece world,

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.090
PERIOD.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:54.949
On the most basic level, this was of course
due to his enormous physical strength - equipped

00:04:54.949 --> 00:05:00.419
with powerful Haki and of course due to his
powerful devil fruit, the Gura-Gura no mi,

00:05:00.419 --> 00:05:04.470
that is said to hold the power to destroy
the entire world.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:09.670
In ALL the encounters he has at marineford,
whether it be Akainu or Blackbeard, he always

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:14.150
seems to have the edge, despite his countless
wounds and illnesses.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:19.020
And of course, we could witness his true power
in his clashes with Oden and Roger, both of

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:23.280
which were considered to be monsters themselves
in terms of brute strength.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:29.550
Additionally, he was a MORE than capable swordsman,
wielding one of the 12 supreme Meito swords,

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.160
that he most likely turned into a black blade
over his lifetime.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:40.250
But beyond these monstrous physical abilities,
Whitebeard also held enormous TACTICAL power.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:45.860
As one of the Yonko, he commanded an enormous
crew and an even larger fleet of affiliated

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.889
pirates.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:52.780
Especially after Roger’s execution and the
end of their rivalry, Whitebeard, who also

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:58.430
had the second highest BOUNTY after Roger,
used his personal AND military power - and

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:03.080
in combination with a very sharp and tactical
mind - to ultimately be the one to control

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:07.729
large parts of the oceans and to keep the
balance in the new world.

00:06:07.729 --> 00:06:13.849
Just HOW strong his grip on the world actually
was, became especially clear after the war,

00:06:13.849 --> 00:06:19.479
where as a result of his death the balance
of the world was dealt a devastating blow.

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:24.409
Countless islands under his protection fell
into anarchy and were invaded by other pirates,

00:06:24.409 --> 00:06:29.509
and the power vacuum he left behind gave room
for new players to gain influence in the new

00:06:29.509 --> 00:06:31.889
world, including the likes of Luffy and Blackbeard.

00:06:31.889 --> 00:06:33.210
"Only the strong chose how they die; weaklings
don't have that right."

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:38.840
And speaking of Whitebeard’s legacy, his
death at Marineford, in my opinion, might

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:44.099
be one of THE most misunderstood scenes in
the entire story.

00:06:44.099 --> 00:06:48.740
Many people like to accuse Whitebeard of not
being the man he once was at Marineford and

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.789
as a result badly overestimating his own strength.

00:06:51.789 --> 00:06:57.120
However, as I see it, Oda made it pretty much
clear, that he never had the intention of

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.570
surviving the war in the first place.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:04.509
Instead, it should be his ultimate proof of
pride and power.

00:07:04.509 --> 00:07:09.360
In other words: Whitebeard went to Marineford
- to die.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:13.319
He purposefully removed the medication he
was hooked to, that was keeping him alive.

00:07:13.319 --> 00:07:18.529
He joined the fight heads on, WITHOUT any
regard for his health or his life to prove

00:07:18.529 --> 00:07:22.240
to the world that he could STILL fight with
the big shots.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:28.069
The thing Whitebeard feared the most was being
pitied for his condition, and so he decided

00:07:28.069 --> 00:07:33.341
that he’d rather go out with a bang rather
than slowly waste away on board of his ship.

00:07:33.341 --> 00:07:38.340
His true intention for the war then, was to
free Ace and make him his successor and the

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:41.039
top candidate for the next pirate king.

00:07:41.039 --> 00:07:47.321
This, in my opinion, is one of the strongest
displays of honour, strength and will we have

00:07:47.321 --> 00:07:51.419
seen in all of one piece outside of the straw
hats.

00:07:51.419 --> 00:07:55.819
Another point I think is important to make
when considering Oda’s portrayal of Whitebeard,

00:07:55.819 --> 00:07:59.580
is his source inspiration for the character.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:04.749
Primarily, there are TWO major characters
who’s attributes have been united in the

00:08:04.749 --> 00:08:05.749
Emperor.

00:08:05.749 --> 00:08:08.729
The first is the real life Blackbeard.

00:08:08.729 --> 00:08:14.699
His character has been an inspiration for
both, White- AND Blackbeard, for two reasons.

00:08:14.699 --> 00:08:20.919
First his name, Edward Teach, which Oda has
split into Edward Newgate and Marshall D.

00:08:20.919 --> 00:08:21.919
Teach.

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:27.800
And secondly, his reputation as one of the
most infamous real pirates in our world.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:32.990
What this shows us, is that Oda has actively
chosen the most recognisable example of a

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:36.669
true pirate as the basis for Whitebeard’s
character.

00:08:36.669 --> 00:08:42.150
But there is second figure, this time from
Japanese folklore, that also plays a major

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:43.150
role here.

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:48.329
I’m speaking of the character of Benkei,
a legendary Japanese warrior monk who was

00:08:48.329 --> 00:08:52.899
said to have lived in the latter years of
the Heian Period in the 12th century.

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:59.279
Benkei was notoriously known for his superhuman
strength as well as his strong sense of loyalty.

00:08:59.279 --> 00:09:05.010
The monk was said to be at least five TIMES
the size of a normal man and wielded a naginata

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:10.630
as his weapon of choice, the same long-range
type of blade as Murakumogiri, the blade that

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:11.850
Whitebeard wields.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:17.959
However, the deed Benkei is MOST known for
is dying against an overwhelming force of

00:09:17.959 --> 00:09:22.920
enemies, standing upright and riddled by arrows
and spears.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:26.300
Oda chose these obvious parallels for a reason.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:32.120
They are what make Whitebeard into the proud,
strong and fearless pirate that he is.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:38.100
Only HE, being Roger’s equal, would have
been able to start a second era of piracy.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:45.820
Because to become pirate king, one needs to
be a true ideal of strength and power.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:53.550
Now, while will-power, strength and influence
are certainly basic requirements for becoming

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:58.440
pirate king, there are actually a number of
candidates that fall into this category, that

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:02.360
literally nobody would want to see on top
of the food chain.

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:03.850
Except for Ryan.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.880
What the hell’s wrong with you Ryan?

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:10.769
So what makes Roger or Luffy different from
say a Blackbeard or a Kaido?

00:10:10.769 --> 00:10:17.060
I would argue that it’s compassion and kindness
that makes for an ideal pirate king, at least

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:20.529
in my and probably also in Oda’s eyes.

00:10:20.529 --> 00:10:26.459
Both, Roger and Luffy represent the quote-unquote
good pirate that helps the weak and strives

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:29.259
for justice, freedom and happiness.

00:10:29.259 --> 00:10:33.600
And that’s what sets them apart from other
strong characters in One Piece.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:38.740
And therefore, I think this also serves as
an argument that Whitebeard also held the

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:44.001
unofficial role of pirate king, as he is not
only an ideal of power and strength but also

00:10:44.001 --> 00:10:45.970
of compassion and kindness.

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:51.210
While he easily could have reached Laugh tale
as well, he never cared to find the one piece

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.480
in the first place.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:58.040
What Newgate was actually looking for was
to form strong relationships and find the

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:01.839
family that he was denied as a child, growing
up as an orphan.

00:11:01.839 --> 00:11:06.591
While we do not know yet, what he was like
during his time with the Rocks pirates, at

00:11:06.591 --> 00:11:11.490
least by the time he started his own crew,
he was a cheerful and carefree young pirate,

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:12.960
roaming the seas.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:16.199
His primary mission in life was protecting
the weak.

00:11:16.199 --> 00:11:21.610
And he did so by putting entire ISLANDS under
his flag and by recruiting lost men into his

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.890
crew by adopting them as his sons.

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:29.480
He did so with Squard, who lost his entire
crew to Roger, with Ace, with Blackbeard and

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:32.610
many others, that didn’t have any other
place to go.

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:38.529
He also did not care much for race or status
and was the only one willing to stand up for

00:11:38.529 --> 00:11:42.769
the fishmen and end their exploitation through
the humans.

00:11:42.769 --> 00:11:47.170
And I think ANOTHER trait that shows whether
someone is a truly great leader is by looking

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:49.390
at how they treat their people.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:54.540
Compared to many of the other Yonko, Whitebeard
had a truly great crew.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:59.069
Kaido seems to rule over his men through power
and fear.

00:11:59.069 --> 00:12:03.649
Blackbeard has surrounded himself with people
hungry for power and blood.

00:12:03.649 --> 00:12:08.490
And Big Mom actually has made her REAL family
into her crew, but doesn’t even get CLOSE

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:12.280
to the level of warmth and joy that the White
Beard Pirates had.

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:17.509
The secret behind this is that Whitebeard
has built his crew predominantly on trust,

00:12:17.509 --> 00:12:19.500
love and respect.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:25.630
Thus, similar to his inspiration Benkei, loyalty
is the major theme of the Whitebeard Pirates,

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:30.290
which is also what makes Blackbeard’s betrayal
of said loyalty the ULTIMATE crime for the

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:31.399
crew.

00:12:31.399 --> 00:12:36.130
And something I feel is directly connected
to this idea, is the strong moral code that

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.449
Newgate has.

00:12:38.449 --> 00:12:42.380
Loyalty &amp; respect are what the Emperor values
most highly.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:46.880
What makes him different from let’s say
Akainu however, who actually shares surprisingly

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:51.449
similar ideals, is that Whitebeard has the
ability to forgive.

00:12:51.449 --> 00:12:58.019
In that sense, the scene with Squard is actually
WAY more important for Whitebeard’s characterisation

00:12:58.019 --> 00:13:00.199
than you might have realised.

00:13:00.199 --> 00:13:04.380
Despite betraying his trust and loyalty, just
as Blackbeard did, and stabbing him through

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:10.990
the back, Whitebeard forgives him by being
compassionate and understanding his true motivation.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:16.440
While Blackbeard betrayed him for power, Squard
was manipulated by Akainu into believing that

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.730
he would be sacrificed for Ace’s sake.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:25.009
The fact that Whitebeard is able to distinguish
between these two cases is pretty much the

00:13:25.009 --> 00:13:31.480
exact opposite to Akainu’s concept of absolute
justice, which is also, why the conflict between

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:34.620
the two works so wonderfully well.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:40.000
They in fact do share a number of views and
values, but in the DECISIVE area of morality,

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.970
they’re the COMPLETE opposite of each other.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:48.680
It is also no wonder then, that Whitebeard
quickly grew to enormously respect Luffy,

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:53.519
Oden and Roger, all of which share these two
fundamental traits of strength and compassion

00:13:53.519 --> 00:13:57.500
as well and could thus change the world for
the better.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:03.060
And this is exactly why I believe that while
he never even tried to find the One Piece,

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:08.220
after Roger’s death, Whitebeard effectively
became the next pirate king and ruler of the

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.319
seas.

00:14:09.319 --> 00:14:14.980
The point here is of course not that Whitebeard
was EXACTLY like Roger, just as Roger was

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:17.270
never exactly like Luffy.

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:21.430
This would not only make little sense, but
would also be extremely boring.

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:22.430
No.

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:27.490
Each of the three has a unique personality
and a unique path to follow.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:32.339
What unites them however, are these central
traits that Oda presents to us as the requirements

00:14:32.339 --> 00:14:34.550
to become the ideal pirate.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:40.870
Or in other words: the stuff that makes a
Pirate King.

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:45.940
So now that we have dissected how Oda has
created the, in my opinion, FANTASTIC character

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:50.629
of Whitebeard in the context of the story,
in the last part of this video, I wanna explore

00:14:50.629 --> 00:14:55.560
how this character ALSO serves as a strong
device for world building.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:59.440
And what we have discussed so far, hopefully
will help you understand better, what makes

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.839
all of this SO genius.

00:15:01.839 --> 00:15:07.440
Because in more than just one way, the introduction
of Whitebeard as a CHARACTER - ALSO introduced

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:12.910
to us several crucial aspects of the One piece
world, that were DESPERATELY needed to progress

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.410
the plot.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:18.949
First of all, Whitebeard introduced us to
the old generation.

00:15:18.949 --> 00:15:23.829
Through his actions and fights, we were able
to witness the monstrous power that the likes

00:15:23.829 --> 00:15:29.210
of Roger, Garp or Rocks must have held when
they were roaming the seas during their prime.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:33.600
It gives us a sense of WAY greater powers
being at work in the one piece world, than

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.880
we originally thought.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:41.370
Physical and political conflicts suddenly
were on a completely different level.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:46.310
And this already brings me to my second point:
Setting a new standard.

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:50.540
This new spectrum of strength and influence
that came with Whitebeard and his war against

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:57.120
the Marines was introduced as a new measuring
stick for Luffy and the crew to strive towards.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:02.360
It showed us how much there still was to learn
and to explore, and how far they still were

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.649
from getting even CLOSE to playing at the
top level.

00:16:05.649 --> 00:16:11.899
In retrospect, it was Oda basically SHOUTING
at us, that a time skip was coming and that

00:16:11.899 --> 00:16:17.149
Luffy needed a significant change in character
AND a new drive to become stronger.

00:16:17.149 --> 00:16:22.579
Whitebeard’s death meanwhile rang in the
end of this OLD era and gave rise to the NEW

00:16:22.579 --> 00:16:26.129
one, making space for Luffy and others to
grow in.

00:16:26.129 --> 00:16:31.329
This of course also included Blackbeard, who’s
character arc in many ways has been about

00:16:31.329 --> 00:16:37.730
opposing and ultimately killing off the last
remaining ideal pirate and thus pushing Luffy

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.670
to fill this newly created vacuum.

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:45.939
So not only did Whitebeard significantly expand
our understanding of the one piece world,

00:16:45.939 --> 00:16:51.250
but he also set up the entirety of the new
world saga by giving the story a fresh start

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:56.860
and at the same time with Blackbeard introducing
the ultimate antagonist for Luffy, that in

00:16:56.860 --> 00:17:01.990
more than just one way can be considered the
anti-pirate king that needs to be kept away

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:05.180
from gaining power at all cost.

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:08.680
After all, what we want is an ideal pirate
king.

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:14.440
What we want is someone as worthy for the
title, as the strongest man in the world.

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:18.770
Another character that has had an enormous
impact on Luffy and his journey, is another

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.370
Emperor: Shanks.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:24.710
You can find out what his role in the story
is, and what role nordic mythology plays for

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.090
his character, by clicking right here.

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:28.090
Peace guys.

